WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.927
A rolling calculation looks at a moving window of values.

00:00:03.927 --> 00:00:11.837
With a window size of three, each rolling mean is based on the current value and the previous two values.

00:00:11.837 --> 00:00:17.840
The first two positions do not yet have three observations, so they appear as missing.

00:00:18.393 --> 00:00:24.780
Rolling averages are useful for smoothing short-term variation and making trends easier to see.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:31.014
Try a window of two or four and compare how quickly the rolling series reacts to changes.
